# Cloned upstream sources — read-only study copies, never committed.
# They belong to their own projects and would bloat this repo's history.
upstream/*
!upstream/README.md
!upstream/repos.txt

# GSD planning workspace — session-local codebase maps and planning state,
# regenerable via /gsd-map-codebase; not part of the repo's public record.
.planning/

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
# Downloaded papers — read-only study copies, never committed.
# Copyright belongs to the publishers; refetchable from each note's arxiv/doi frontmatter.
references/papers/pdf/*
!references/papers/pdf/.gitkeep

# Cached vendor model cards. NOT refetchable the way a paper is — a card is rewritten in
# place at one URL — which is why every card note carries a REQUIRED snapshot: (Wayback)
# URL. The note plus its snapshot is the record; this copy is a convenience.
references/cards/pdf/*
!references/cards/pdf/.gitkeep
# Generated SQLite export of the corpus — a VIEW over frontmatter, never authoritative
# (ADR-0035). Rebuilt from scratch in under a second by scripts/build-db.py, so it is
# never worth committing and never worth repairing: delete and rebuild.
comparisons/repo.db

# Probe wire evidence (Phase 9, D-09 one-way-door checkpoint). RESEARCH/ARCHITECTURE's
# default was "committed, not gitignored" (dated primary evidence, like experiments/
# logs), but on 2026-09-01 the owner declined that default for now: "I am not
# comfortable right now. Can we gitignore it now? Maybe I will change it later."
# PROVISIONAL — revisit at Phase 11 before the contract sweep commits its evidence
# base. Consequence accepted meanwhile: rule-4 traceability for probe_id citations is
# broken until this policy flips — a probe_id in Phase 11's classified YAML may not be
# resolvable by a repo reader. probes/harness/ (code) and probes/sets/ (declarations)
# are NOT covered by this rule and are committed normally.
probes/raw/
probes/ledger.jsonl

__pycache__/
